Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Load-up checks: spread the delayed load-up scan over
 several frames

OnDelayedWorldLoadFinished ran the role, recovery, outfit, lot object and inventory checks and then the dereference controllers' first pass over every reference collected at load, all in one frame, before the first sleep inside ObjectLookup.BuildReference. In our profiles that is one 0.5-0.9 s frame one sim-minute after every load (7 of 7 measured loads), about three quarters in CheckInventories and the rest in the controllers' PreProcess pass.

The checks now share an existing SleepWatch: a sleep after the role/recovery/outfit/lot checks, one after the inventory check, and one between controller items, each only once the frame has used the new kScanSleepInterval tunable (default 10 ms, ErrorTrapTuning7). The scan already lets other work run in between (BuildReference sleeps between and inside controller items), so these are more of the same kind of sleep points; every check and controller does the same work in the same order. Set kScanSleepInterval to 0 for the old one-frame run.

Assisted with AI
